# Build outputs and installed trees. These are regenerated inside the image, and
# the frontend stage installs dependencies in a layer of its own — without this
# file the later `COPY frontend/ .` puts the host's node_modules straight back on
# top of it, so the image ships whatever the developer happened to have. CI never
# saw it because a fresh checkout has none of these; a local build did.
#
# pnpm's node_modules is a tree of symlinks into node_modules/.pnpm, which does
# not survive being copied out of context, so this stops being a wasted layer and
# starts being a broken build.
node_modules/
target/
dist/
.angular/

# Test artefacts, never part of a release image.
test-results/
playwright-report/

.git/
result
